# Okra

## Variable

```okra
let v Type = value;
let v = value;
```

## With-expression

```okra
let p = Point{ x = 0; y = 1 }
let pp = p with { .x = 1 }
```

## Function

```okra
fn name() do end
fn name() Type do end
fn name(p Type) Type do end
fn name(p Type, p Type) Type do end
fn name(p Type, p ...Type) Type do end
```

### Split Function

```okra
fn name(p Type) other(p Type) do end
fn name(p Type) other(p Type) Type do end
fn name(p Type) other(p Type) yet_another(p Type) Type do end
fn name(p Type, p Type) other(a Type) yet_another(p Type) Type do end
```

### Block Function

```okra
fn name() b block() do end
fn name() b block() Type do end
fn name() b block(p Type) Type do end
fn name() b block(p Type, p Type) Type do end
fn name() b block(p Type, p ...Type) Type do end
```

#### Slit Block Function

```okra
fn name(p Type) b block(p Type) other(p Type) Type do end
fn name(p Type) other(p Type) b block(p Type) Type do end
fn name(p Type) b block(p Type) other(p Type) b block(p Type) Type do end
```

## Type

### Function Type

```okra
let f fn(Type) Type = value;
```

### Union types

```okra
type X union
  Int;
  String;
  end
```

### Type alias

```okra
type IntOperator fn(Int, Int)Int end
type Email String end
```

## Enum

```okra
type Gender enum
  Male;
  Female;
  end
```

An enum item may be a value of any type

```okra
type X enum
   x X = 10;
   x = true;
   end
```

An enum item's value may be an anonymous record

```okra
type[T] Planet enum[mass T, radius T]
  Mercury[Float, Float]{ mass Float = 3.3, radius Float = 2.4 };
  Venus{ mass = 4.8; radius = 6.5 };
  Earth{ mass = 5.9; radius = 6.3 };
  Mars{ mass = 6.2; radius = 3.3 };
  Jupiter{ mass = 1.9; radius = 7.1 };
  Saturn{ mass = 5.6; radius = 6.0 };
  Uranus{ mass = 8.6; radius = 2.5 };
  Neptune{ mass = 1.0; radius = 2.4 };
  Pluto{};
  end
```

## Record

```okra
type Name record
  c T;
  c T;
  end
```

## Interface

```okra
type Name interface
  fn name(T, T) T end
  fn name(T) other(T) T end
  fn name(T, T) block() T end
  end
```

## Case function set

```okra
type Conditional case
  fn ifTrue() block() end
  fn ifFalse() block() end
  end
```

A case-function set may also have normal functions

```okra
type Greeting case
  fn englishGreeting(String) String end
  fn spanishGreeting(String) String end
  end
```

A type implements a case-function set by implement one
and only one of the methods in the case-function set.

> A `union` type implements a case-function set if all its
> subtypes implements the case-function set.
> Same for an `enum`, if all its item types implements the
> case-function set.

## Method

```okra
fn o Type name(t T) T do end
fn _ Type name(t T) T do end
```

## Enum item method

```okra
fn o enum(T.T) name(t T) T do end
fn o T.T name(t T) T do end
fn o T:T name(t T) T do end
fn o T where T T.T name(t T) T do end
```

## Constructor

```okra
fn t T new() T do end
fn t T new() T b block() do end
```

## Generics

### Generic Function

```okra
fn[T, T] name(t T, x X) T do end 
fn[T, T] name(t T, x X) other(p T) T do end 
fn[T, T] name(t T, x X) b block(T) T do end
```

### Generic Type

#### Generic Record

```okra
type[T, T] Name record
  name T;
  end
```

### Generic Enum

```okra
type[T] Name enum
   name[Int] = 10;
   name[Bool] = true;
   name record[Int]{ item X = value; }
   end
```

#### Generic Interface

```okra
type[T, T] Name interface
  fn name(T) T end
  fn name(T) block(T) T end
  end
```

#### Generic Case function

```okra
type[T, T] Name case
  fn name(T) T end
  end
```

#### Generic Method

```okra
-- (1) method for any instance of type P
fn[T] p P[T] name(t T) T do end

-- (2) method for only instances of type P[Int]
fn p P[Int] name(t T) T do end
```

#### Generic Function Type

Can only be defined inside a generic method

```okra
fn[T] p P[T] name() do
  let f f(T) T = value;
  end
```
